---
/**
 * The full palette catalog with infinite scroll.
 *
 * This is what the home page used to be. It moved here when the home page
 * became a landing: a visitor arriving at the root wants to see what the site
 * is, while a visitor who clicks Explore wants to browse without interruption.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Feed from '../../components/Feed.astro';
import { getFirstRows, getMeta, SSG_BATCH } from '../../lib/data.server.js';

const meta = getMeta();
const chunks = meta.feeds?.new?.chunks ?? 0;
const preRows = getFirstRows('new', SSG_BATCH);
const tagCount = meta.tags.length;

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://palette-vault.example');
const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${site.origin}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Palettes' },
    ],
  },
  {
    '@type': 'CollectionPage',
    name: 'Color palettes',
    description: 'Browse every four-color palette in the catalog, free to copy and use.',
    url: `${site.origin}/palettes/`,
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Browse All Color Palettes — Free to Copy | Palette Vault"
  description={`Explore every color palette in the catalog, built in OKLCH. Click a swatch `
    + `to copy its HEX, save the ones you like, or filter by ${tagCount} categories.`}
  active="new"
  schema={schema}
>
  <Feed
    title="Browse all color palettes"
    subtitle="Every four-color palette, newest first. Click any swatch to copy its HEX."
    type="chunks"
    base="/data/new"
    chunks={chunks}
    preRows={preRows}
    emptyTitle="No palettes yet"
    emptyText="Run npm run generate to build the dataset."
  >
    <div slot="intro" class="page-intro">
      <p>
        Every palette here is four colors chosen to work together. Click a
        swatch to copy its HEX code, or open a palette to take all four at once
        as RGB, CSS variables or a JSON array, and download it as a PNG.
      </p>
      <p>
        The feed loads as you scroll, so there is no pagination to work
        through. Narrow it down using the {tagCount} categories in the sidebar,
        or jump to a specific{' '}
        <a href="/colors/" title="All color names with hex codes">color</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="page-note">
      <h2>What holds these palettes together</h2>
      <p>
        Every palette is built in <strong>OKLCH</strong>, a perceptually uniform
        color space: an equal step in lightness looks like an equal step to the
        eye, which is not true in RGB or HSL. That is what keeps a four-color
        set feeling related rather than merely varied.
      </p>
      <p>
        The four hues follow a classical relationship — monochrome, analogous,
        complementary, split complementary, triad or tetrad — instead of sitting
        at arbitrary angles. Lightness runs as a ladder from light to dark, so
        there is always somewhere to put text. And chroma tapers at both
        extremes, because very light and very dark colors hold less of it, which
        is what stops the pale end going chalky and the dark end turning muddy.
      </p>

      <h2>Sorting and saving</h2>
      <p>
        This page is ordered newest first. <a href="/popular/">Popular</a> ranks
        by likes, <a href="/random/">Random</a> reshuffles on every visit, and
        anything you like lands in <a href="/collection/">your collection</a>,
        which is stored in your own browser rather than on a server.
      </p>
    </section>
  </Feed>
</Layout>
